> A peak intersection is only a candidate

The native `dtmf_peaks()` helper finds the first maximum in each four-frequency
group. It does not test whether an adequate tone exists in both groups. Silence
therefore yields candidate '1' by ties. A single row tone, a signal containing
two column tones, or a block too short to separate the grid also yields some
candidate. Displaying that character does not validate the signal.

[ITU-T Q.24 (11/1988), Section 2](https://www.itu.int/rec/T-REC-Q.24-198811-I/en)
identifies reception parameters beyond a maximum search, including simultaneous
group presence, frequency tolerances, levels and timing. Chen’s SPRA066 likewise
assumes prior tone and timing validation and explicitly describes its detector
as incomplete. The following are controlled counterexamples, not conformance tests.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/goertzel_candidates.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/goertzel.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <limits>
#include <numbers>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

 const std::vector<std::string> labels{"Quiet","One row","Pair 5","Two cols","N = 8"};
 const std::vector<std::vector<double>> signals{std::vector<double>(410,0),dm::algorithms::sinusoid_signal(410,8000,{{770,1,0}}),dm::algorithms::dtmf_signal('5',410),dm::algorithms::sinusoid_signal(410,8000,{{770,1,0},{1209,1,0},{1477,1,0}}),dm::algorithms::dtmf_signal('5',8)};
 std::vector<double> row,col;
 std::print("| signal | samples | candidate | chosen row Hz | chosen column Hz | row peak | column peak |\n| --- | ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
 for(std::size_t i=0;i<signals.size();++i){const auto p=dm::algorithms::dtmf_peaks(signals[i]);
  row.push_back(p.responses[p.row].power);col.push_back(p.responses[4+p.column].power);
  std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {:.0f} | {:.0f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} |\n",labels[i],signals[i].size(),p.candidate,p.target_hz[p.row],p.target_hz[4+p.column],row.back(),col.back());
 }
 auto a=dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot(row,labels),b=dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot(col,labels);
 a.title("Largest row response").xlab("").ylab("Raw power").y_limits(0,50000);
 b.title("Largest column response").xlab("").ylab("Raw power").y_limits(0,50000);
 dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(a).add(b).size(1100,500).title("Every block has peak indices; that alone does not validate a key").fit_panels().save_svg("build/goertzel_candidates.svg");
 if(dm::algorithms::dtmf_peaks(signals[0]).candidate!='1')throw std::runtime_error("silence tie");

}
