> Count selected updates, not hardware time

Each target uses N recurrence updates and constant working state. M independent
targets use MN updates, plus sample validation, target selection, trigonometric
setup and terminal evaluation. The source recurrence has one product, an addition
and a subtraction per sample; compiler contraction and machine instructions are
not measured by the update counter.

A complete FFT has a different operation mix and produces an entire spectrum.
O(MN) versus O(N log N) describes scaling, not an exact timing crossover at
M=log N and not a proof that eight Goertzel passes are always faster. The experiment
below counts actual updates from repeated native calls. Input storage and retained
trace records are separate from ordinary constant working state.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/goertzel_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/goertzel.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <limits>
#include <numbers>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

 const auto grid=dm::algorithms::dtmf_peaks({});
 std::vector<double> x;std::vector<std::vector<double>> y(4);
 std::print("| samples N | targets M | predicted updates | actual updates |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
 for(std::size_t n:{16u,32u,64u,128u,256u,512u,1024u,2048u,4096u}){
  const auto signal=dm::algorithms::dtmf_signal('5',n);x.push_back(std::log2(double(n)));
  for(std::size_t j=0;j<4;++j){const std::size_t m=std::size_t{1}<<j;std::size_t updates=0;
   for(std::size_t i=0;i<m;++i)updates+=dm::algorithms::goertzel_run(signal,grid.target_hz[i],8000).sample_updates;
   std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",n,m,n*m,updates);y[j].push_back(std::log2(double(updates)));
   if(updates!=n*m)throw std::runtime_error("actual update count");
  }
 }
 auto p=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
 p.line(x,y[0],"1",{5,150,105},2).points(x,y[0],"1",{5,150,105},3)
  .line(x,y[1],"2",{37,99,235},2).points(x,y[1],"2",{37,99,235},3)
  .line(x,y[2],"4",{217,119,6},2).points(x,y[2],"4",{217,119,6},3)
  .line(x,y[3],"8",{220,38,38},2).points(x,y[3],"8",{220,38,38},3)
  .legend({"1 target","2 targets","4 targets","8 targets"},{{5,150,105},{37,99,235},{217,119,6},{220,38,38}})
  .title("Actual recurrence updates equal samples × targets").xlab("log2(samples N)").ylab("log2(actual sample updates)")
  .x_limits(4,12).y_limits(0,17).save_svg("build/goertzel_work.svg");

}
```
