// result_end
\caption(The signed errors and negative raw power are retained. In the right panel the exact positive bar is too small to resolve on this scale; its nonzero value is printed. No epsilon floor, absolute-value repair or zero clamp is applied.)
\alttext(One panel shows signed relative DC errors for ten block lengths up to one million samples. The other compares negative raw power with positive exact DC power after an explicitly stated scaling. The printed large-index response exposes loss of ideal alias periodicity.)

Nonfinite samples, invalid rates, unsafe legacy integer conversions and evaluated
nonfinite states or terminal outputs are rejected. These checks prevent invalid
values from propagating; they do not certify the accuracy of finite results.
Empty input returns zero after parameter validation, with no coefficient evaluated.
This is finite-block processing, not an automatically sliding transform or an
infinite-duration streaming receiver.

> Bound complete histories and whole generated signals separately

Trace quotas count complete initial, sample and stop records online. N=4 therefore
needs six records, and empty input needs two metadata records. The optional quota
is checked before each whole append; zero disables the quota while still recording.
No numerical replay, truncated history or partial result is returned.

Input/root/ordinary result and selection metadata/constant working states/
allocator overhead are excluded. A record quota is not numeric entries, bytes or
peak RAM. Signal generation instead admits its whole output sample count before
allocation, after validating all descriptors. Both units differ from recurrence
updates, despite similarly named numeric limits.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/goertzel_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/goertzel.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <limits>
#include <numbers>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

 const std::vector<double> x{1,2,3,4};const auto original=x;
 bool record_rejected=false,empty_rejected=false,signal_rejected=false,invalid_before_quota=false,conversion_rejected=false,overflow_rejected=false;
 try{(void)dm::algorithms::goertzel_bin_trace(x,0,5);}catch(const std::length_error&){record_rejected=true;}
 const auto t=dm::algorithms::goertzel_bin_trace(x,0,6);
 try{(void)dm::algorithms::goertzel_bin_trace({},0,1);}catch(const std::length_error&){empty_rejected=true;}
 const auto empty=dm::algorithms::goertzel_bin_trace({},0,2);
 try{(void)dm::algorithms::sinusoid_signal(4,8,{{1,1,0}},3);}catch(const std::length_error&){signal_rejected=true;}
 const auto signal=dm::algorithms::sinusoid_signal(4,8,{{1,1,0}},4);
 try{(void)dm::algorithms::goertzel_bin_trace({1,2,std::numeric_limits<double>::quiet_NaN()},0,1);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){invalid_before_quota=true;}
 try{(void)dm::algorithms::goertzel_power({1,2},1e300,1);}catch(const std::overflow_error&){conversion_rejected=true;}
 try{(void)dm::algorithms::goertzel_power_bin({1e308,1e308},0);}catch(const std::overflow_error&){overflow_rejected=true;}
 auto copy=t;copy.events[1].value=999;
 std::print("| resource | retained amount | rejected limit | rejected |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |\n| Four-sample complete history | {} | 5 | {} |\n| Empty initial and stop metadata | {} | 1 | {} |\n| Whole generated signal | {} | 3 | {} |\n",t.events.size(),record_rejected,empty.events.size(),empty_rejected,signal.size(),signal_rejected);
 std::print("\nZero optional history quota retains {} records; zero optional signal quota generates {} samples. Independent owned copy {}; invalid last sample before quota {}; unsafe bin conversion rejected {}; nonfinite state rejected {}; caller input unchanged {}.\n",dm::algorithms::goertzel_bin_trace(x,0,0).events.size(),dm::algorithms::sinusoid_signal(4,8,{{1,1,0}},0).size(),t.events[1].value!=copy.events[1].value,invalid_before_quota,conversion_rejected,overflow_rejected,x==original);
 auto a=dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot({double(t.events.size()),5.},{"Retained","Rejected cap"});
 a.title("Online actual history").xlab("").ylab("Complete records").y_limits(0,8);
 auto b=dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot({double(signal.size()),3.},{"Generated","Rejected cap"});
 b.title("Whole generated signal").xlab("").ylab("Output samples").y_limits(0,6);
 dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(a).add(b).size(1100,500).title("Complete records and generated samples have separate quotas").fit_panels().save_svg("build/goertzel_controls.svg");
 if(!record_rejected||!empty_rejected||!signal_rejected||!invalid_before_quota||!conversion_rejected||!overflow_rejected)throw std::runtime_error("resource/domain controls");

}
```
